    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0550" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/923c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Fletcher</hi>)<anchor n="3" xml:id="d385-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-04T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1924—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>72. On May 14 the French, British and Spanish Governments deposited at Paris the
                    ratifications of the Convention regarding the <pb facs="0551" n="457"
                        xml:id="pg457"/> Organization of the Statute of the Tangier Zone signed at
                    Paris December 18, 1923, and they have now requested the adhesion of the
                    Government of the United States as one of the signatories of the Act of
                        Algeciras.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d385-f2"/> Please endeavor informally to
                    ascertain the attitude of the Italian Government towards this Convention, as
                    well as to the Tangier Port Concession of December 11, 1923,<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d385-f3"/> and report as to whether the Italian Government appears
                    disposed to adhere to the Convention with or without conditions or
                    reservations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d385-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d385-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis,</hi> to the representatives
                    in Belgium (no. 45), the Netherlands (no. 23), and Portugal (no. 23).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d385-f2" n="4" xml:id="d385-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="frus1906p2#pg_1495"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1906, pt. 2, p. 1495</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d385-f3" n="5" xml:id="d385-f3-content">
                <p>Additions made to the original concession of June 2, 1921. For correspondence
                    concerning the 1921 concession, see <ref target="frus1922v02#pg_720"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1922, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ii</hi>, pp. 720</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
